v2.14.0 — TencentDB Agent Memory absorptions (2026-05-24)
================================================================================

Tencent/TencentDB-Agent-Memory
  https://github.com/Tencent/TencentDB-Agent-Memory
  License: NOASSERTION upstream (README shows an MIT badge; actual LICENSE
  file lists no SPDX identifier). Treated as idea-level adoption only —
  no upstream code was copied. Two new policies and two zero-dep Node
  scripts re-implement the patterns from scratch to fit the kit's
  infrastructure-free model.
  Adapted (v2.14.0):
    (1) Symbolic memory — Mermaid canvas + `node_id` drill-down for
        long-horizon agents (50+ tool calls). Documented in
        `policies/symbolic-memory.md`; reference implementation in
        `scripts/mmd-canvas-builder.mjs` (zero-dep, reads
        `.auto/tool-calls.jsonl`, emits `.auto/canvas.mmd` plus
        `.auto/refs/Nk.md`). Cross-link in
        `skills/40-parallel-dispatcher/SKILL.md`.
    (2) Memory pyramid — L0 (Conversation) → L1 (Atom) → L2 (Scenario) →
        L3 (Persona) layering, mapped onto our existing 4-tier model in
        `policies/memory-tiers.md`. Documented in
        `policies/memory-pyramid.md`; L3 generator in
        `scripts/l3-persona-generator.mjs` (zero-dep, reads
        `memory/*.md` atoms + `architecture/<project>/decisions.md`
        scenarios). Wired into `commands/consolidate-memory.md` as
        optional step 6.5.
  We do NOT adopt:
    - The TypeScript runtime (`src/`) and its OpenClaw/Hermes plugin
      lifecycle hooks. We have no plugin gateway to host such a runtime.
    - The sqlite-vec storage and BM25 + embedding + RRF hybrid recall.
      The vault stays as inspectable markdown; grep + wikilinks remain
      the recall mechanism.
    - The DeepSeek-V3.2 / OpenAI-compatible LLM extractor invoked for
      automatic L1/L2 extraction. Our consolidation stays semi-manual
      via `/consolidate-memory`, preserving zero per-session cost and
      auditability.
    - The Docker Hermes deployment (`docker/Dockerfile.hermes`) and
      the gateway HTTP API.
    - Automatic context-window monitoring with `mildOffloadRatio` /
      `aggressiveCompressRatio` thresholds. Activation in the kit is
      explicit (heuristics documented in the policy, decision made by
      the orchestrator), not driven by a state machine.

